WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.775
Unit 4 is the logs, before the pilot.

2
00:00:02.775 --> 00:00:07.946
Learn says the service keeps traffic and
remote network health logs for thirty days;

3
00:00:07.946 --> 00:00:11.713
longer retention needs export
through diagnostic settings.

4
00:00:11.713 --> 00:00:16.909
So a dedicated Entra diagnostic setting
sends four categories to the workspace:

5
00:00:16.909 --> 00:00:20.010
network access traffic
logs, connection events,

6
00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:23.500
remote network health logs,
and network access alerts.

7
00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:26.575
Sign-in and audit logs
stay on the core setting.

8
00:00:26.575 --> 00:00:31.733
A freshness query runs daily, and a
sudden drop in traffic volume is an alert

9
00:00:31.733 --> 00:00:36.725
in itself, because it covers offboarding,
a disabled profile, or an outage.

10
00:00:36.725 --> 00:00:38.213
And there's a federal reason.

11
00:00:38.213 --> 00:00:42.717
CISA's Remote User Use Case says that
as users connect more directly to

12
00:00:42.717 --> 00:00:48.062
external services, CISA's visibility must
be preserved through telemetry sharing.

13
00:00:48.062 --> 00:00:52.963
Moving users off a full-tunnel V P N
moves their telemetry to Microsoft,

14
00:00:52.963 --> 00:00:56.513
so agree how it reaches
CISA with the agency's tick

15
00:00:56.513 --> 00:00:59.780
delegates before the V P
N's web path is retired.
